.TH SDL_LoadFunction 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_LoadFunction \- Look up the address of the named function in a shared object.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_loadso.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_FunctionPointer SDL_LoadFunction(SDL_SharedObject *handle, const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function pointer is no longer valid after calling
.BR SDL_UnloadObject ()\[char46]
.PP
This function can only look up C function names\[char46] Other languages may have name mangling and intrinsic language support that varies from compiler to compiler\[char46]
.PP
Make sure you declare your function pointers with the same calling convention as the actual library function\[char46] Your code will crash mysteriously if you do not do this\[char46]
.PP
If the requested function doesn\(aqt exist, NULL is returned\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I handle
a valid shared object handle returned by
.BR SDL_LoadObject ()\[char46]

.TP
.I name
the name of the function to look up\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the function or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_LoadObject (3)
